docs\plans\DESIGN-CONVERSION-SERVER-ILEARNINGMACHINE-PLAN-v1.md:106:| Stage 9 - Training and evaluation runbook | Define measured training loop with speed, accuracy and visual quality evidence. | `30.DesignConversionDomain`, `11.DPO`, `04.TrainingLoop`, `models`, `training-data` | `design-conversion-training-runbook-GUIDE.md`, translation runbook, small model rationale | Training runner, eval runner, run report, held-out set, ablation report | UML for training/eval flow; algorithm for batch -> update -> metrics; code quotes for DPO/training interfaces | Speed, preference accuracy, visual quality, held-out, ablation, fresh-load, continue-training, regression | Training can pass by memorizing deterministic/source shortcuts | Converts accepted rows into model evidence | No external AI |
docs\plans\DESIGN-CONVERSION-SERVER-ILEARNINGMACHINE-PLAN-v1.md:734:Accepted rows train; held-out rows never train; quarantine rows never train. Chosen/rejected examples from Stage 8 feed DPO. Regression example: a batch improves reward margin but worsens visual held-out score, so it is rollback/quarantine, not promotion.
