docs\plans\evidence\extension-full-readiness-dual-path\phase-13-hidden-deterministic-shortcut-review.md:50:| SkillSelection candidate-position weights | `43.SmartSkillsDomain/SkillSelectionMachine.cs:101-102` "Candidate-position scaffold weights updated"; `SkillSelectionMachine.cs:128-142` "diagnostics and leakage-guard evidence only"; `SkillSelectionLogicalHierarchy.cs:322-327` "candidate_order_guard_status=selection_authority_blocked" | Learns `_candidatePositionWeights`, then blocks using them as final authority; evaluates permutation probes via semantic-unit path without candidate position. | Candidate order/position is exactly a shortcut vector; current guard reduces risk but does not prove all trained selection behavior is source-disjoint. | `ILogicalUnit` guard/helper and `ILearningMachine` training diagnostic only. | MEDIUM | Source-disjoint SkillSelection eval and candidate-order/position ablation tied to positive behavior. | Future bounded SkillSelection shortcut-ablation packet with candidate order permutations, decoy requested-skill controls, and row-level leakage ledger. | Do not claim candidate-position shortcut fully excluded; may claim only guard/scaffold is labelled non-authoritative. |
docs\plans\evidence\extension-full-readiness-dual-path\phase-13-hidden-deterministic-shortcut-review.md:51:| SkillSelection prompt/task/context/intermediate dictionaries | `SkillSelectionMachine.cs:980-1003` prompt/context features feed typed `PromptContextSkillSelectionUnit`; `SkillSelectionMachine.cs:2740-2767` extracts prompt, host, project-root, provenance signals; `SkillSelectionMachine.cs:2868-2911` rejects `SemanticQualityClaimed` in every unit section. | Stores learned feature dictionaries and source-pair ids across prompt/task/context/intermediate skill states, with semantic-quality flags forced false. | Prompt/context/provenance features can become hidden keyword/provenance shortcuts unless splits and ablations prove generalization. | `ILogicalUnit` typed baseline evidence; dictionary state is allowed only as transparent learned-signal support. | HIGH | Source-pair leakage audit, prompt/context/provenance ablations, and held-out source-family split. | Future bounded leakage review over all SkillSelection feature dictionaries, including prompt/context/intermediate units and source-pair provenance. | Do not call dictionary match semantic understanding or quality improvement. |
docs\plans\evidence\extension-full-readiness-dual-path\phase-13-hidden-deterministic-shortcut-review.md:52:| SkillSelection TryDecideWith* chain | `SkillSelectionMachine.cs:173-215` chain checks `TryDecideWithSkillSelection`, `PromptContext`, `ResultGap`, `OutputValidation`, `TaskCompletion`, `IntermediateChecks`, `SkillCandidates`, `Routing`, `TaskType`, `TaskUnderstanding`, `PromptUnderstanding`; `SkillSelectionMachine.cs:945-977` labels typed unit selection and candidate-position scaffold non-authoritative. | Prioritizes typed semantic units before falling back to candidate-position diagnostic guard; each unit returns evidence and false semantic-quality claims. | Chain ordering can hide deterministic helper precedence unless every unit's feature authority is audited. | `ILogicalUnit` chain within `ILearningMachine` selection machine. | OK | Complete unit-by-unit shortcut map and eval/ablation evidence for each active decision path. | Future bounded chain-order audit after positive eval artifacts exist. | Do not claim chain order proves no shortcut; it proves only explicit non-authority labels in reviewed paths. |
docs\plans\evidence\extension-full-readiness-dual-path\phase-13-hidden-deterministic-shortcut-review.md:55:| source-pair/provenance leakage risk | `SkillSelectionMachine.cs:1819-1847` keeps `_sourcePairIdsBySkill` and KNN examples; `SkillSelectionMachine.cs:2760-2765` adds `provenance_ref_present` and `provenance_ref_structured`; `PromptToTaskTaskPatternUnit.cs:363-404` quarantines evidence-only authority text. | Tracks source pair ids and provenance markers; PromptToTask has current-unquoted authority handling and evidence-only quarantine. | Source/pair/provenance can leak target labels or scenarios unless excluded from final authority and ablated. | Provenance is allowed as audit metadata and authority hygiene signal, not final selection/routing authority. | HIGH | Explicit leakage ledger proving source ids, pair ids, scenario ids, provenance keys, and file paths cannot determine outputs. | Future bounded provenance-leakage packet across SkillSelection, PromptToTask, and OrchestrationReasoning. | Do not call provenance hygiene a source-disjoint proof. |
docs\plans\evidence\extension-full-readiness-dual-path\phase-13-hidden-deterministic-shortcut-review.md:56:| KNN/retrieval helper boundary | `SkillSelectionLogicalHierarchy.cs:1190-1212` finds nearest skill-candidate examples; `SkillSelectionLogicalHierarchy.cs:1281-1288` says `knn_role=support_evidence_only`; `PromptToTaskTaskPatternUnit.cs:281-285` says nearest/KNN overlap is transparent baseline, not semantic quality. | KNN/retrieval-like helpers support evidence and baseline scoring while reporting semantic quality false. | Retrieval helper can masquerade as semantic reasoning if report wording or downstream gates ignore helper-only status. | `ILogicalUnit` helper/baseline only. | MEDIUM | End-to-end evidence that helper-only outputs never open quality/readiness and are ablated against non-retrieval baselines. | Future bounded helper-boundary audit after eval packets exist. | Do not claim KNN/retrieval success as learned semantic quality. |
docs\plans\evidence\extension-full-readiness-dual-path\phase-13-hidden-deterministic-shortcut-review.md:57:| report wording/claim strength | `PromptToTaskMachine.cs:204-206` emits `BASELINE_NOT_SEMANTIC_QUALITY`, `SEMANTIC_QUALITY_CLAIMED_FALSE`; `OrchestrationReasoningMachine.cs:597-602` emits baseline/host/semantic false evidence; `SkillSelectionMachine.cs:2868-2911` rejects unit semantic quality claims. | Current wording repeatedly downgrades baseline/helper outputs and rejects semantic-quality flags in checkpoints/manifests. | Wording is protective, but wording alone does not prove hidden shortcuts absent. | Reporting contract only; no implementation or eval claim. | OK | Report must stay linked to row-level evidence and not upgrade to closed until eval/ablation pass. | Keep Phase 13.01 as intake; next phase can document status only after parent review. | Do not phrase this as "risk closed"; phrase as "claim remains closed". |
