docs\plans\EXTENSION-RUNTIME-TOKEN-QUALITY-LEARNABILITY-EXECUTION-STATE.json:3079:    "cycle_06_finding": "Cycle 6 found that the plan had a human-readable quality rubric, but quality improvement and semantic quality claims needed a concrete machines/layers -> inputs -> scoring criteria -> fail labels -> artifacts matrix. Section 4.3 now requires PromptToTask, OrchestrationReasoning, SkillSelection and final usefulness to be scored on the same paired baseline/adaptive scenarios after pairing integrity passes; source-disjoint held-out prompts; positive/negative examples from real reviewed references where available; reviewer notes; regression guard; ablation/no-leakage/no-memorization controls; and quality non-regression before token savings. Full semantic quality, common readiness, target promotion and locator update remain closed when any layer only shows narrow staged, baseline-only, deterministic-only, test-only, one-host or one-machine improvement.",
