docs\plans\EXTENSION-RUNTIME-TOKEN-QUALITY-LEARNABILITY-EXECUTION-STATE.json:3975:    "finding_summary": "PLAN-REVIEW-05 found that the quality requirements were named in the target matrix and final-readiness gates, but Section 4.3 did not yet force a saved quality eval prompt pack with source-disjoint metadata and real-reference positive/negative examples before scoring. The repair adds quality-eval-prompt-pack.md/jsonl, source-disjoint row fields, positive/negative real-reference example rules, per-layer coverage for PromptToTask, OrchestrationReasoning, SkillSelection and final usefulness, an inconclusive-quality continue/fix path, and a stronger final acceptance quality row. Token savings, smoke/runtime success, static evidence, and generic scoring cannot substitute for quality improvement."
